 {:db/id "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd10be9b-3b17-5633-861a-6fa42ef0e0d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/ef6b3c8a066aa4f14722d27e35b31ab6414cf6cba0ded8a063a0b53e18174200" "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/c8a139a7781cbf1484c5c65d833041ae69c859d2c77c229a5e0cb871eee8b46b" "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/eb17b3e164dea3327acae3b877cd3aefdf4b9450fb5eb47b0f9c4fa4f660223e" "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a"] :answer-field/correct "q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e/b9248a6ddaa63032886818da7db1f1bcca7b4af333798c69a62e6a3c7eb9a71a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-338623" :question/id #uuid "dc494029-58f4-51d4-95fe-9c9b2384d2b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-338623" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)={x}^{2},\\,y(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=1$ and $x=b=3.$\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6\n$$\n\nThese are Robin (mixed) boundary conditions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338623/ma-source-field/e7b134718f960463b9bc9935de2e6aa70368a930584c41c4e42a232a7bc6fd9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
