 {:db/id "q-33987" :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33987/ma-source-field/1a8a1907879a570ee0fb24b3e23ba1b0dada92402bb96e92fcf3415d711d0d94"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
