 {:db/id "q-34361" :question/id #uuid "cade4505-b877-5cb5-ae1c-bc1354365d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34361" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}41 \\\\ 82\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{2}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34361/ma-source-field/f0b8a32ffa34c17e3e8317194cfb84f6f85e8223aa8ca7af917061f7c63df4e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
