 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "de878af4-60e8-5b69-ad9a-b8c3044d2e69"] :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50}=1$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35410/ma-source-field/cfd9f45d2c4ac865e1c34144bdf0b54bf1afa86bb064bc571dcf8e0e279c7443"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
