 {:db/id "q-35527" :question/id #uuid "fb8b2d04-67d4-51d3-8ebf-71fc804b1a61" :question/math-academy-id "q-35527" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\nII. $c=-1$ gives a parabola\nIII. $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy=\\pm 1,$ which are hyperbolas.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35527/ma-source-field/4b3e96482e4abb4f8c8238a77cccc85b79bf02384437382f2551991dfc5a2d16"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
