 {:db/id "q-35577" :question/id #uuid "69276016-ba7c-50d9-a595-a7d6a823a97c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35577" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic paraboloid $z=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{27}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{27} \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{27}(y-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35577/ma-source-field/8bf46699b01833590c7f8fd04ee36f176912fd542c342b281984d9058491038f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
