 {:db/id "q-35731" :question/id #uuid "719356e3-8c2f-52eb-b04e-5bd8a3bf6ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35731" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35731/ma-source-field/bd7147ead04e58af5737222f37bf18d9658ae379685ac2806c3b44583d93cbfb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
