 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "c93d2ae4-7e7b-5500-9b27-fd939892ffa9"] :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35732/ma-source-field/b4566feea09bf00becb8e68f5d48bf2cfb98126f2350a30eed9435fa71f88e44"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
